# rules: swift-command-from-untrusted-input
# languages: swift
# fixture: swift/CWE-78.swift
# from: CWE-78 (OS Command Injection), CWE-88
#
# `Process` with `-c` hands the whole of its argument to a shell, so a `;`, a
# backtick or a `$(...)` anywhere in it starts a second command with the app's
# privileges. This is macOS Swift rather than iOS - a sandboxed iOS app cannot
# spawn a process at all - and it is the same weakness there that it is
# everywhere else.
#
# The fix is the default. `executableURL` plus an `arguments` array never
# involves a shell, so a semicolon in an argument is a semicolon; only the
# explicit `sh -c` spelling reintroduces one.
#
# The rule wants two things at once and asks for both, because either alone
# reports the wrong thing. A `-c` in the arguments with nothing untrusted in it
# is a fixed command line and is not a finding; an untrusted value in an
# arguments array with no `-c` is passed to `execve` as one argument and is
# also not a finding. It is the pair that is the bug, so the guard reads the
# array for the shell flag and `reaching` asks whether anything the caller
# chose ended up in it.
#
# The whole array is the sink rather than one element. That is deliberate: the
# assembled command may be built by interpolation, by concatenation or in a
# variable a line above, and the array is the one span all three end up in.

["$$$T.arguments = $ARGS", "$$$T.setArguments($ARGS)"] as $runs
| [ "$$$U.lastPathComponent", "$$$U.pathComponents", "$$$U.absoluteString",
    "$$$U.queryItems", "$$$U.fragment", "UIPasteboard.general.string",
    "$$$F.text", "$$$P.string(forKey: $K)" ] as $untrusted
| "\"-c\"|\"-ec\"|\"/c\"" as $throughAShell
| scan_ast("*.swift"; $runs + $untrusted) as $all
| ( $all | of($runs)
    | where_capture("ARGS"; $throughAShell)
    | focus("ARGS")
    | reaching($all | of($untrusted); []) )
| finding("swift-command-from-untrusted-input";
    "this goes to a shell with `-c`, so a `;` or a backtick in the value the "
    + "caller chose starts a second command; pass the program and its "
    + "arguments separately instead")
| report
